WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back!
-Thank you!

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So happy to have you here.
-I'm happy to be here.

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.538 size:78% position:39%
-I want to talk about
this wonderful film,

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.407 size:78% position:39%
but I would be remiss
not to ask you this,

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:09.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I know we talked
about "The Sopranos"

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:11.111 size:88% position:44%
last time you were here.
It's just been announced

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:15.215
David Chase is going to make a
prequel movie to "The Sopranos,"

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:16.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
called
"The Many Saints of Newark."

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that as exciting to you
as it is to me?

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:21.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's already
more than I knew.

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:23.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I didn't know the title.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I should have said,
"Spoiler alert."

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.960
-Yeah.
-I feel like I didn't realize --

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A little late for that.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:30.730
-But -- No, I just found out
about it like everybody else.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:34.667
It's, you know, the story,
I guess, of Tony's parents

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Uncle Junior
when they were kids.

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:39.072
-So, there's no baby Carmela?
You don't have to worry about --

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:41.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I put in
my picture and résumé.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.176 size:75% position:38%
That's all I can do.
-Okay, that's great.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
This is a wonderful film.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is -- you play
a high school teacher

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:50.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
who is helping an ex-student
get out of jail.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-And doing advocacy work

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
despite the fact
that you have

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
your own family
and your own job.

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:55.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
What drew you
to a role like this?

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:59.125
-I worked with Jay Duplass --
sort of worked with him --

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.127 line:92%
on a movie called "Landline."

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
We weren't in scenes together,
but I met him

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's just charming and
darling and sweet.

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:06.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And a wonderful actor, yeah.
-And a fantastic actor.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:09.769 size:88% position:44%
They said he co-wrote it
and was starring in it,

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.571 line:92%
which was amazingly great.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.872 line:92%
And then I read the script,

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's the way
people really talk

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it seemed to be
the way people really live.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's the kind of stuff
I respond to,

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that was it.
-That's fantastic.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know one thing that it had
that you don't love is

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:24.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
you actually had to go to
Washington state to shoot it.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.586 line:92%
-Yes. Big challenge for me.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because you love
being in New York, right?

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:30.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I would like to say
that's what it is.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:33.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's more that I don't
like being somewhere else.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha. That --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, i just don't like
leaving home.

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:38.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I have a family
and a life here.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.033 size:84% position:42%
And it's different from
when I was a little kid

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was like, you know,
"Pack your bag,

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:44.304
and we're going to shoot a movie
in, you know, Timbuktu.

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:45.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's just
those days are gone.

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.941
-Right. You like being home.
You like being in New York.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you have been in New York
for a long time.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:52.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Long time.
-I read an interview with you,

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:54.547
and I was thrilled to hear
the way that you used to

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:57.517
get around New York City,
which is rollerblades.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:58.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-Is this true?

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For many, many years.
-Wow, wow!

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:03.990
-Rollerblades and chain smoking.
-Wow, that is --

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It really was like...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:08.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
Seriously. Seriously.
-I feel like there was, like,

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:12.365
a day where both of those became
outlawed in New York.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:13.633 line:92%
It was, like, the same day.

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it didn't matter to me
at all, though.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.603 size:78% position:39%
It took me many years
to stop both of them.

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.538 size:75% position:38%
-I was going to say,
it seems dangerous

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:19.339 line:92%
to rollerblade in New York.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
But if you were already
smoking a cigarette, like...

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:22.475 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:23.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were obviously
looking death in the eye.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Some sort of a death wish,
I guess.

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:28.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, for years I did that.
-And now a Vespa.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is that active?
Are you still...

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah, yeah.
I used it this afternoon.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:33.853 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I use it all the time.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's the best way
to get around the city.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:36.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're in and out of
appointments.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
You pull between two cars,
you know?

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:42.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just great.
-And you -- your kids --

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.329 line:92%
Was there a time in your life

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.231
when your kids would ride
on the Vespa with you?

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
Would you have a kid
on the back?

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.101 size:88% position:44%
The time was -- Today,
this afternoon, in fact.

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:49.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow! That's great.
-Yeah, it is great.

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:52.639
I love it. You don't go --
You never get to go really fast.

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:53.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-You know?

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You must have a great
relationship with your kids

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.477
if they're willing to jump
on the back of the Vespa

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:58.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
with their mom.
I think that's a very...

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, they don't do it
willingly.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:02.916 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Mind you.

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:03.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, they actually
get a kick out of it.

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.185 size:88% position:44%
-Well, I just feel bad
'cause they probably get

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:07.887
all the cigarette smoke, right?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:11.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's funny.
-Oh, thank you.

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:11.824 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm just sayin'.

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:14.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, do they --
they're 13 and 10?

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:15.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Son's 13, right?

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-Acting bug?

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:18.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not at all, no.
-Really?

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.334
-I don't know even know if they
know that's what I do.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:21.901 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:22.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I just have
weird hours,

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:25.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I come home and
i have a lot of makeup on.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But they don't ask, you know.
-Uh-huh.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:30.143
-They saw me on a bus once, and
they were a little suspect,

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they didn't pursue it.
-Gotcha.

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you think it is
that they pursue?

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:35.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
What are the -- At those ages,
what do they want To be?

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:37.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My son wants to be
a soccer star.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:40.286
I'm not entirely sure he won't.
He's very good.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, that's exciting.
-I dare say.

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:45.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
My daughter wants to be
a pop star and a veterinarian.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:46.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's nice.
-So...

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:47.293 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:48.595 line:92%
By the time she's of age,

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:50.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
those two things
may somehow be combined.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
-You're a dog lover.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:54.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm a big animal lover, yeah.
-I have a dog, as well.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
You took your dog
to a dog psychic.

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:59.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No!
-You didn't?

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:01.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That would make more sense.
-Okay.

00:04:01.608 --> 00:04:03.243 line:92%
-I spoke to a woman on the phone

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was in, I'm going to say,
North Dakota.

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:06.346 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:09.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I think I had to send her
a picture first.

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:10.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-And that's what we did.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:13.953
-Oh, wait, so, she told you
what your dog was thinking

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:16.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
off a photo?
Why didn't she just --

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:16.990 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Can i just tell you?

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:19.659
This dog was a little teeny dog
I had rescued.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:22.262
-Okay.
-And she was sick all the time.

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:25.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it turned out,
I found out later on,

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:26.366 size:81% position:41% line:92%
that she was pregnant,

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:27.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she had been a mommy
in a puppy mill.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:30.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, anyway, it was
a long, ugly story.

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:32.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I asked the woman,
she said, "Wait,

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:35.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
she's saying to me, 'They're
taking my babies,'

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:37.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
your dog is saying."
Which she knew

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:39.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
that my dog had been a mom,
like, many times.

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:42.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was crazy weird that
this woman knew these things.

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:43.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I don't know.

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:46.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I totally bought it,
hook, line, and sinker.

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:47.754 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:49.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn't pay.
I didn't pay anything.

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did-- Okay,
well, now, that --

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:53.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-None the wiser.
I mean phone bill.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.727 line:92%
-So, this person just is, like,

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:57.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
running a terrible business
where...

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:57.930 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:58.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't think
it's her business.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
It might just be, like,
a little side thing he does.

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:03.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
-How did you find her?

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:07.373
-It was at somebody's --
like a -- I don't know --

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:08.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
a baby shower.
-Uh-huh.

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:10.643 size:84% position:42%
-And a woman said, "Oh,
I know a dog psychic."

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:12.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it went like that.
I don't know.

00:05:12.412 --> 00:05:13.179 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:15.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There was nothing
up until that point?

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:17.517
Nothing came up before that?
-You know, I barely remember

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:19.819 size:75% position:38%
my children's names,
so give me a minute.

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:21.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was something like that.
-Gotcha.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:22.188 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:23.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One thing that obviously
keeps you in New York

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:26.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
is when you do stuff --
stage stuff here.

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:27.193 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:28.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know you've done a lot
in the past.

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:29.462
Do you have anything coming up?
Is that something

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
you'd like to do again?
-I do, in fact.

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:31.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to be doing a play
with the new group

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:34.400
in September, called "The True."
-That's exciting.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I don't even know if
I'm supposed to say that yet.

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:37.337 size:81% position:41%
-Oh, that's exciting!
-But i just did, so...

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:38.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
-There you have it.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now it's out there.
-Yeah.

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:41.240 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You know who...

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.943 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:46.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
I actually already
knew about it,

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:49.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I talked to this woman
in North Dakota.

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:51.117 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:53.086
I sent her -- Just before
I interview someone --

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:54.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sent a picture of me.
-I sent her a picture of you.

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:56.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's so good.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:57.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's like, "I don't know
about the dog,

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:59.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
but Edie is doing a play."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:01.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
"That much I know."
-Thank you so much

00:06:01.461 --> 00:06:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
for being back.
-So happy to be here.

